IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `psga-directions`

-- Public Sector (Governance) Act 2018 (Singapore) -- Part 3 (personnel) and Part 4
-- (governance: conflicts of interest and decision-making), ss 12 to 32, with the
-- transitional rules in s 45 that bear on Part 3.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules
-- skill. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate.

§ `Public Sector (Governance) Act 2018 -- Parts 3 and 4`

§§ `12, 22 -- who Parts 3 and 4 apply to`

-- s 12: "This Part applies to and in relation to every Group 1, every Group 2 and every
-- Group 3 public body to the extent provided in this Part." s 22: the same for Part 4.
--
-- Group 2 and Group 3 carry the main-function condition (see psga-directions.l4), so a body
-- listed in Part 1 of the Second Schedule whose main function is not regulating a
-- profession is a Group 2A public body and is outside both Parts, although s 15 names
-- Group 2A.
GIVEN `the body` IS A BodyFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Parts 3 and 4 apply to the body` IF
    `the body is a Group 1, 2 or 3 public body` `the body`

§§ `14 to 19 -- chief executives`

-- s 15(1): "the chief executive of a Group 1, Group 2A or Group 3 public body MUST BE
-- APPOINTED BY THE PUBLIC BODY, and no other."
-- s 15(2): "An individual must not be appointed as the chief executive of a Group 1, Group 2A
-- or Group 3 public body except -- (a) with the PRIOR APPROVAL of the responsible Minister
-- ..., in the case of a Group 1, Group 2A or Group 3 public body; and (b) with the PRIOR
-- CONCURRENCE of the Public Service Commission, in the case of a GROUP 1 public body."
-- s 15(3): where an individual has been appointed in contravention of (2), "the responsible
-- Minister ... may issue a direction to the public body to remove the individual ...; and the
-- public body must comply with that direction."
--
-- GROUP 2B IS NOT NAMED. A Group 2B chief executive is subject to no rule in this Division,
-- and a Group 3 body's chief executive needs the Minister's approval and no one else's.
-- s 2(1) "appoint" (s 13) includes appointing a public officer under a secondment
-- arrangement but excludes promoting.
DECLARE ChiefExecutiveFacts HAS
    `the body` IS A BodyFacts
    `the appointment was made by the public body` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the responsible Minister gave prior approval` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Public Service Commission gave prior concurrence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the chief executive was appointed before 1 April 2018 and held office immediately before that date` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the chief executive is a public officer under a secondment arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN

-- The bodies ss 15 and 16 name: Group 1, Group 2A and Group 3. Part 3 must also apply (s 12).
GIVEN `the body` IS A BodyFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `sections 15 and 16 apply to the body` IF
        `Parts 3 and 4 apply to the body` `the body`
    AND (    `the body is a Group 1 public body` `the body`
         OR  `the body is a Group 2A public body` `the body`
         OR  `the body is a Group 3 public body` `the body`)

-- s 45(2): "Section 15 does not apply to any individual who -- (a) is appointed as the chief
-- executive of a public body before 1 April 2018; and (b) is holding that office immediately
-- before that date."
GIVEN `the chief executive` IS A ChiefExecutiveFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 15 governs this appointment` IF
        `sections 15 and 16 apply to the body` (`the chief executive`'s `the body`)
    AND NOT `the chief executive`'s `the chief executive was appointed before 1 April 2018 and held office immediately before that date`

GIVEN `the chief executive` IS A ChiefExecutiveFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appointment complies with section 15` IF
    IF   NOT `section 15 governs this appointment` `the chief executive`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE     `the chief executive`'s `the appointment was made by the public body`
         AND `the chief executive`'s `the responsible Minister gave prior approval`
         AND (    NOT `the body is a Group 1 public body` (`the chief executive`'s `the body`)
              OR  `the chief executive`'s `the Public Service Commission gave prior concurrence`)

-- s 15(3): a contravening appointment can be unwound by a Ministerial direction, with which
-- the public body "must comply".
GIVEN `the chief executive` IS A ChiefExecutiveFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the responsible Minister may direct the public body to remove the chief executive` IF
        `section 15 governs this appointment` `the chief executive`
    AND NOT `the appointment complies with section 15` `the chief executive`

-- s 16(1): "the chief executive of a Group 1, Group 2A or Group 3 public body must not be
-- removed from that office except -- (a) with the prior approval of the responsible Minister
-- ...; and (b) with the prior concurrence of the Public Service Commission, in the case of a
-- Group 1 public body."
-- s 16(2): (1) does not apply where "(a) a direction is given by a responsible Minister under
-- section 15(3); or (b) the Public Service Commission concurs under section 17 with a
-- DISMISSAL of a chief executive of a Group 1 public body."
-- s 16(3): this does not prevent a RESIGNATION or its acceptance.
--
-- So a Group 1 chief executive dismissed for misconduct needs only the Commission's
-- concurrence under s 17; one removed for any other reason needs both the Minister's approval
-- and the Commission's concurrence. A Group 2A or Group 3 chief executive dismissed for
-- misconduct needs the Minister's approval only: s 17 does not reach them.
-- s 45(3): ss 16 and 18 apply to a chief executive holding office on 1 April 2018, although
-- s 15 does not.
DECLARE RemovalFacts HAS
    `the chief executive` IS A ChiefExecutiveFacts
    `it is a resignation or the acceptance of one` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it follows a direction by the responsible Minister under section 15(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is a dismissal to which the Public Service Commission concurred under section 17` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the responsible Minister gave prior approval` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Public Service Commission gave prior concurrence` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the removal` IS A RemovalFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the removal complies with section 16` IF
    IF   NOT `sections 15 and 16 apply to the body` (`the removal`'s `the chief executive`'s `the body`)
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE     `the removal`'s `it is a resignation or the acceptance of one`
         OR  `the removal`'s `it follows a direction by the responsible Minister under section 15(3)`
         OR  (    `the body is a Group 1 public body` (`the removal`'s `the chief executive`'s `the body`)
              AND `the removal`'s `it is a dismissal to which the Public Service Commission concurred under section 17`)
         OR  (    `the removal`'s `the responsible Minister gave prior approval`
              AND (    NOT `the body is a Group 1 public body` (`the removal`'s `the chief executive`'s `the body`)
                   OR  `the removal`'s `the Public Service Commission gave prior concurrence`))

-- s 17(1): "A disciplinary penalty must not be imposed by any GROUP 1 public body on its chief
-- executive without the prior concurrence of the Public Service Commission with the decision".
-- s 13: "'disciplinary penalty', for a chief executive, means dismissal from the office of chief
-- executive, reduction in grade, financial penalty, stoppage of increment or withdrawal of any
-- employment benefit BECAUSE OF MISCONDUCT".
-- s 17(2): not for a chief executive who is a public officer under a secondment arrangement.
-- s 45(4): s 17 does not apply to a penalty resulting from (a) disciplinary proceedings
-- started before 1 April 2018 or (b) proceedings for misconduct carried out before that date,
-- "even if disciplinary proceedings start on or after that date".
--
-- Only Group 1. The same dismissal by a Group 2A body is a removal under s 16 and not a
-- disciplinary penalty under s 17 in effect, because s 17 does not name Group 2A.
DECLARE PenaltyFacts HAS
    `the chief executive` IS A ChiefExecutiveFacts
    `it is a dismissal, reduction in grade, financial penalty, stoppage of increment or withdrawal of an employment benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is because of misconduct` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the disciplinary proceedings started before 1 April 2018, or concern misconduct before that date` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Public Service Commission gave prior concurrence` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the penalty` IS A PenaltyFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `this is a disciplinary penalty within section 13` IF
        `the penalty`'s `it is a dismissal, reduction in grade, financial penalty, stoppage of increment or withdrawal of an employment benefit`
    AND `the penalty`'s `it is because of misconduct`

GIVEN `the penalty` IS A PenaltyFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 17 requires the Public Service Commission's concurrence` IF
        `this is a disciplinary penalty within section 13` `the penalty`
    AND `Parts 3 and 4 apply to the body` (`the penalty`'s `the chief executive`'s `the body`)
    AND `the body is a Group 1 public body` (`the penalty`'s `the chief executive`'s `the body`)
    AND NOT `the penalty`'s `the chief executive`'s `the chief executive is a public officer under a secondment arrangement`
    AND NOT `the penalty`'s `the disciplinary proceedings started before 1 April 2018, or concern misconduct before that date`

GIVEN `the penalty` IS A PenaltyFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the penalty complies with section 17` IF
        NOT `section 17 requires the Public Service Commission's concurrence` `the penalty`
    OR  `the penalty`'s `the Public Service Commission gave prior concurrence`

-- s 18(1): "A Group 1 public body must not promote its chief executive to a higher grade in
-- that office without the prior concurrence of the Public Service Commission".
-- s 18(2): where promoted in contravention, the responsible Minister "may give a direction to
-- the public body to take such steps as are necessary to rectify the contravention; and the
-- public body must comply with that direction DESPITE ANY AGREEMENT OR OTHER LAW."
-- s 18(3): not for a seconded public officer.
--
-- The seconded public officer is outside ss 17 and 18 but INSIDE ss 15 and 16: there is no
-- secondment exception for appointment and removal.
DECLARE PromotionFacts HAS
    `the chief executive` IS A ChiefExecutiveFacts
    `the Public Service Commission gave prior concurrence` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the promotion` IS A PromotionFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the promotion complies with section 18` IF
        NOT `the body is a Group 1 public body` (`the promotion`'s `the chief executive`'s `the body`)
    OR  `the promotion`'s `the chief executive`'s `the chief executive is a public officer under a secondment arrangement`
    OR  `the promotion`'s `the Public Service Commission gave prior concurrence`

GIVEN `the promotion` IS A PromotionFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the responsible Minister may direct the body to rectify the promotion` IF
    NOT `the promotion complies with section 18` `the promotion`

-- s 19: "this Division does not affect any requirement in the Constitution for the concurrence
-- of the President to an appointment or a removal of the chief executive of a public body in
-- the Fifth Schedule to the Constitution."
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `this Division relieves a requirement for the President's concurrence under the Constitution` IF
    FALSE

§§ `20, 21 -- deemed public servants and public officers`

-- s 20(1): "The following individuals of a Group 1, Group 2 or Group 3 public body are each
-- deemed to be a PUBLIC SERVANT for the purposes of the Penal Code 1871 in relation to his or
-- her carrying out any function of the public body: (a) the chairperson; (b) a member; (c) the
-- chief executive; (d) an officer".
-- s 20(2): "Every member of a COMMITTEE which -- (a) is formed by a GROUP 1A, GROUP 1B, GROUP 2
-- or GROUP 3 public body; and (b) is DELEGATED to carry out any function of the public body ...
-- is taken to be a public servant".
-- s 21(1): every individual mentioned in s 20, "and every member of a committee which is formed
-- by a GROUP 1C public body to carry out any of its functions", is taken to be a PUBLIC OFFICER
-- for the purposes of the Financial Procedure Act 1966 in relation to (a) administering,
-- assessing, collecting or enforcing payment of any fee, tax, charge, financial penalty or
-- other sum imposed or collected under the constitutional Act or other written law, where
-- collected as agent of the Government or payable into the Consolidated Fund or another
-- Government Fund; (b) disbursing, on behalf of the Government, financial assistance or other
-- benefits from the Consolidated Fund or another Government Fund; or (c) administering and
-- managing a contract entered into or managed by the body on behalf of the Government.
-- s 21(2): every member and officer of a Group 1 public body with a function of acting as an
-- agent of the Government is, in entering into contracts on behalf of the Government in the
-- performance of that function, a public officer for the purposes of the Government Contracts
-- Act 1966.
--
-- THE GROUP 1C GAP. A committee of a Group 1C public body (the People's Association alone)
-- is a committee whose members are public OFFICERS under s 21(1) and whose members are NOT
-- deemed public SERVANTS under s 20(2), which names Groups 1A, 1B, 2 and 3 and omits 1C. The
-- Penal Code consequences of being a public servant are lost and the Financial Procedure Act
-- ones gained.
--
-- A purely ADVISORY committee is outside s 21(1) too: it speaks of a committee "formed ... to carry
-- out any of its functions", and an advisory committee carries out none. That is a reading.
DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `the chairperson`
    `a member`
    `the chief executive`
    `an officer`
    `a member of a committee delegated a function of the public body`
    `a member of a committee that only advises the public body`
    `a contractor to the public body`

DECLARE CommitteeBodyFacts HAS
    `the body` IS A BodyFacts
    `the committee was formed by the body` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the role` IS A Role, `the committee body` IS A CommitteeBodyFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the individual is deemed a public servant under section 20` IF
    CONSIDER `the role`
    WHEN `the chairperson` THEN `the body is a Group 1, 2 or 3 public body` (`the committee body`'s `the body`)
    WHEN `a member` THEN `the body is a Group 1, 2 or 3 public body` (`the committee body`'s `the body`)
    WHEN `the chief executive` THEN `the body is a Group 1, 2 or 3 public body` (`the committee body`'s `the body`)
    WHEN `an officer` THEN `the body is a Group 1, 2 or 3 public body` (`the committee body`'s `the body`)
    WHEN `a member of a committee delegated a function of the public body`
        THEN     `the committee body`'s `the committee was formed by the body`
             AND (    `the body is a Group 1A public body` (`the committee body`'s `the body`)
                  OR  `the body is a Group 1B public body` (`the committee body`'s `the body`)
                  OR  `the body is a Group 2 public body` (`the committee body`'s `the body`)
                  OR  `the body is a Group 3 public body` (`the committee body`'s `the body`))
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the role` IS A Role, `the committee body` IS A CommitteeBodyFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the individual is taken to be a public officer under section 21(1)` IF
        `the individual is deemed a public servant under section 20` `the role` `the committee body`
    OR  (    `the committee body`'s `the committee was formed by the body`
         AND `the body is a Group 1C public body` (`the committee body`'s `the body`)
         AND `the role` EQUALS `a member of a committee delegated a function of the public body`)

DECLARE FinancialProcedureActFunction IS ONE OF
    `administering, assessing, collecting or enforcing payment of a sum collected as agent of the Government or payable into a Government Fund`
    `disbursing financial assistance or other benefits on behalf of the Government from a Government Fund`
    `administering and managing a contract entered into or managed on behalf of the Government`
    `any other function`

GIVEN `the function` IS A FinancialProcedureActFunction
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the deeming in section 21(1) reaches this function` IF
    CONSIDER `the function`
    WHEN `any other function` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `23 -- when a member is interested in a relevant matter`

-- s 23(1): "'relevant matter', for a public body, means -- (a) the public body's performance of
-- its functions or exercise of its powers under written law; or (b) an arrangement or
-- agreement, or a contract, made or entered into, or PROPOSED to be made or entered into, by
-- the public body."
-- s 23(2): "A member of a public body is interested in a relevant matter ... if the member, OR
-- AN ASSOCIATE OF THE MEMBER -- (a) may derive a direct or indirect financial benefit from the
-- relevant matter; (b) may have a direct or indirect financial interest in a person to whom the
-- relevant matter relates; or (c) is otherwise directly or indirectly interested in the matter."
-- s 23(3): "However, a member ... is not interested ... in a relevant matter -- (a) ONLY BECAUSE
-- of an interest in a question about the level of remuneration, allowances or expenses to be set
-- for members; (b) only because of an interest ... shared in common with the general public or a
-- substantial section of the public; (c) only because [of] ... payment or reimbursement of
-- membership fees for, or expenses related to membership in, a body with predominantly
-- charitable objects; (d) only because he or she has past or current involvement in the
-- relevant sector, industry or practice; (e) only because ... a customer of any service provided
-- or goods supplied by the public body to the public generally ...; (f) only because the member
-- is a director or chief executive officer of a wholly-owned subsidiary corporation of the public
-- body and the relevant matter is with or for the benefit of or done on behalf of that
-- subsidiary; (g) where the member is appointed to represent the Government or a holder of a
-- public office, or a community or special interest group ..., only because the relevant matter
-- is with or for the benefit of ... that body; or (h) if his or her interest is SO REMOTE OR
-- INSIGNIFICANT that it cannot reasonably be regarded as likely to influence him or her".
--
-- Limbs (a) to (g) each take away one GROUND of interest ("only because"); limb (h) takes away
-- the interest altogether. A member with a financial benefit ground AND an excepted ground is
-- still interested, because the financial ground is untouched.
DECLARE InterestGround IS ONE OF
    `a direct or indirect financial benefit from the relevant matter`
    `a direct or indirect financial interest in a person to whom the relevant matter relates`
    `some other direct or indirect interest in the matter`
    `an interest in the level of remuneration, allowances or expenses for members`
    `an interest shared in common with the general public or a substantial section of it`
    `payment or reimbursement of fees or expenses of a body with predominantly charitable objects`
    `past or current involvement in the relevant sector, industry or practice`
    `being a customer of the public body's services or goods supplied to the public`
    `being a director or chief executive officer of a wholly-owned subsidiary of the body, where the matter is for that subsidiary`
    `being appointed to represent the Government, a public office or a community group, where the matter is for that body`

GIVEN `the ground` IS AN InterestGround
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `this ground is excepted by section 23(3)(a) to (g)` IF
    CONSIDER `the ground`
    WHEN `a direct or indirect financial benefit from the relevant matter` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a direct or indirect financial interest in a person to whom the relevant matter relates` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `some other direct or indirect interest in the matter` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the grounds` IS A LIST OF InterestGround
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `some ground survives the exceptions` IS
    CONSIDER `the grounds`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN FALSE
    WHEN `g` FOLLOWED BY `rest`
        THEN     (NOT `this ground is excepted by section 23(3)(a) to (g)` `g`)
             OR  `some ground survives the exceptions` `rest`

DECLARE MemberInterest HAS
    `the matter is a relevant matter of the public body` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the grounds of interest, whether the member's or an associate's` IS A LIST OF InterestGround
    `the interest is so remote or insignificant that it cannot reasonably be regarded as likely to influence the member` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the interest` IS A MemberInterest
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the member is interested in the relevant matter` IF
        `the interest`'s `the matter is a relevant matter of the public body`
    AND `some ground survives the exceptions` (`the interest`'s `the grounds of interest, whether the member's or an associate's`)
    AND NOT `the interest`'s `the interest is so remote or insignificant that it cannot reasonably be regarded as likely to influence the member`

§§ `23(4) -- associates`

-- s 23(4): "a person is an associate of another if -- (a) they are spouses or siblings or a parent
-- and child or they are in a similar close family relationship; (b) they are in partnership; (c)
-- one is a company and the other is a director or manager of the company; (d) one is a PRIVATE
-- company within the meaning of the Companies Act 1967 and the other is a SHAREHOLDER in the
-- company; or (e) a CHAIN OF RELATIONSHIPS can be traced between them under one or more of the
-- above paragraphs."
--
-- THE CHAIN HAS NO LENGTH LIMIT, and limb (d) has no minimum shareholding. A member who holds
-- one share in a private company is an associate of the company, so a company that contracts
-- with the public body is an associate who may derive a financial benefit, and the member is
-- interested -- unless the interest is so remote that s 23(3)(h) takes it away. A shareholder
-- of a PUBLIC company is not caught by (d).
DECLARE RelationshipKind IS ONE OF
    `spouses, siblings, parent and child, or a similar close family relationship`
    `in partnership`
    `a company and a director or manager of it`
    `a private company and a shareholder in it`
    `a public company and a shareholder in it`
    `no relationship`

GIVEN `the kind` IS A RelationshipKind
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `this link is one that section 23(4) recognises` IF
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `spouses, siblings, parent and child, or a similar close family relationship` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `in partnership` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a company and a director or manager of it` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a private company and a shareholder in it` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the chain` IS A LIST OF RelationshipKind
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `every link in the chain is recognised` IS
    CONSIDER `the chain`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN TRUE
    WHEN `k` FOLLOWED BY `rest`
        THEN     `this link is one that section 23(4) recognises` `k`
             AND `every link in the chain is recognised` `rest`

-- An empty chain is not a relationship at all.
GIVEN `the chain` IS A LIST OF RelationshipKind
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the two are associates` IS
    CONSIDER `the chain`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE `every link in the chain is recognised` `the chain`

§§ `23(5) -- "wholly-owned subsidiary corporation of a public body"`

-- s 23(5): "a person is a wholly-owned subsidiary corporation of a public body if none of the
-- members of the corporation is a person other than -- (a) the public body; (b) a nominee of the
-- public body; (c) a subsidiary of the public body being a subsidiary none of the members of
-- which is a person other than that public body or a nominee of that public body; or (d) a
-- nominee of a subsidiary mentioned in paragraph (c), and 'subsidiary' has the meaning given by
-- the Companies Act 1967."
--
-- THIS IS THE SAME FORMULA AS COMPANIES ACT 1967 s 5B AND HAS THE SAME DEFECT. Limb (c) admits a
-- subsidiary only if its own members are the public body or the body's nominee. In the chain
--      public body -> S2 -> S1 -> C
-- the corporation C has the single member S1, whose single member is S2. S1 fails limb (c), so C
-- is not a wholly-owned subsidiary corporation of the public body. A director of C is not within
-- the s 23(3)(f) exception, although every share in the chain is held by the one body.
DECLARE Occupant IS ONE OF
    `the public body itself`
    `a nominee of the public body`
    `a subsidiary of the public body`
    `a nominee of a subsidiary of the public body`
    `any other person`

GIVEN `who` IS AN Occupant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the occupant is the public body or its nominee` IF
    CONSIDER `who`
    WHEN `the public body itself` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a nominee of the public body` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

DECLARE Member HAS
    `who it is` IS AN Occupant
    `the members of the subsidiary concerned` IS A LIST OF Occupant

GIVEN `the occupants` IS A LIST OF Occupant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `every occupant is the public body or its nominee` IS
    CONSIDER `the occupants`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN TRUE
    WHEN `o` FOLLOWED BY `rest`
        THEN     `the occupant is the public body or its nominee` `o`
             AND `every occupant is the public body or its nominee` `rest`

GIVEN `the member` IS A Member
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 23(5) admits this member` IF
    CONSIDER `the member`'s `who it is`
    WHEN `the public body itself` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a nominee of the public body` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a subsidiary of the public body`
        THEN `every occupant is the public body or its nominee` (`the member`'s `the members of the subsidiary concerned`)
    WHEN `a nominee of a subsidiary of the public body`
        THEN `every occupant is the public body or its nominee` (`the member`'s `the members of the subsidiary concerned`)
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the members` IS A LIST OF Member
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the corporation is a wholly-owned subsidiary corporation of the public body` IS
    CONSIDER `the members`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN TRUE
    WHEN `m` FOLLOWED BY `rest`
        THEN     `section 23(5) admits this member` `m`
             AND `the corporation is a wholly-owned subsidiary corporation of the public body` `rest`

§§ `24, 25 -- the duty to disclose, and to whom`

-- s 24(1): "A member of a public body who is interested in a relevant matter relating to the
-- public body MUST DISCLOSE details of the interest in accordance with section 25 AS SOON AS
-- PRACTICABLE after the member becomes AWARE that he or she is interested."
-- s 24(2): a general notice of an interest in a relevant matter, including one that "may IN
-- FUTURE relate to the public body", disclosed under s 25 is a STANDING DISCLOSURE.
-- s 24(3): "a standing disclosure CEASES TO HAVE EFFECT if the nature of the interest MATERIALLY
-- ALTERS or the extent of the interest MATERIALLY INCREASES."
--
-- A decrease in the extent does not end the standing disclosure; a change in nature does, in
-- either direction.
-- s 24(4): this is in addition to any rule of law restricting a member from having interests in
-- conflict with his or her duties.
DECLARE StandingDisclosure HAS
    `a general notice was disclosed in accordance with section 25` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the nature of the interest has materially altered` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the extent of the interest has materially increased` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the extent of the interest has decreased` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the disclosure` IS A StandingDisclosure
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the standing disclosure is still effective` IF
        `the disclosure`'s `a general notice was disclosed in accordance with section 25`
    AND NOT `the disclosure`'s `the nature of the interest has materially altered`
    AND NOT `the disclosure`'s `the extent of the interest has materially increased`

-- s 25(1): "A member of a public body who is interested ... must disclose details of the interest
-- -- (a) in the case of the CHAIRPERSON -- (i) to the chief executive and all other members of
-- the public body; and (ii) to the responsible Minister for the public body; or (b) in the case
-- of ANY OTHER MEMBER -- (i) to the chairperson of the public body; (ii) if there is no
-- chairperson or the chairperson is interested, to a deputy chairperson of the public body; or
-- (iii) if there is neither a chairperson nor deputy chairperson or if the chairperson and every
-- deputy chairperson are interested, to the responsible Minister".
--
-- THE LADDER OVERLAPS. Where the chairperson is interested, (ii) says to disclose to a deputy
-- chairperson, and nothing in (ii) requires the deputy to be disinterested. Where the chairperson
-- AND every deputy are interested, (ii) still applies by its terms, and so does (iii). And where
-- there is NO chairperson but a deputy exists who is interested, (ii) applies and (iii) does not
-- ("the chairperson and every deputy chairperson are interested" is not satisfied if there is no
-- chairperson to be interested), so the disclosure goes to an interested deputy.
-- s 25(2): the details are (a) the nature and monetary value of the interest if it can be
-- quantified, or (b) the nature and extent if not.
DECLARE Board HAS
    `there is a chairperson` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the chairperson is interested` IS A BOOLEAN
    `there is a deputy chairperson` IS A BOOLEAN
    `every deputy chairperson is interested` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the board` IS A Board
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an ordinary member must disclose to the chairperson` IF
    `the board`'s `there is a chairperson`

GIVEN `the board` IS A Board
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an ordinary member must disclose to a deputy chairperson` IF
        (    NOT `the board`'s `there is a chairperson`
         OR  `the board`'s `the chairperson is interested`)
    AND `the board`'s `there is a deputy chairperson`

GIVEN `the board` IS A Board
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an ordinary member must disclose to the responsible Minister` IF
        (    NOT `the board`'s `there is a chairperson`
         AND NOT `the board`'s `there is a deputy chairperson`)
    OR  (    `the board`'s `there is a chairperson`
         AND `the board`'s `the chairperson is interested`
         AND `the board`'s `there is a deputy chairperson`
         AND `the board`'s `every deputy chairperson is interested`)
    OR  (    `the board`'s `there is a chairperson`
         AND `the board`'s `the chairperson is interested`
         AND NOT `the board`'s `there is a deputy chairperson`)

-- The chairperson's own disclosure is to two audiences.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the chairperson must disclose to the chief executive and all other members, and to the responsible Minister` IF
    TRUE

-- s 25(3): "The chief executive ... must ensure that every disclosure under this section -- (a)
-- is recorded in a register of interests kept by the public body; and (b) is brought to the
-- attention of the member presiding at a meeting ... that relates to the relevant matter."
DECLARE ChiefExecutiveDuty HAS
    `the disclosure is recorded in the register of interests` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was brought to the attention of the member presiding at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the duty` IS A ChiefExecutiveDuty
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the chief executive has done what section 25(3) requires` IF
        `the duty`'s `the disclosure is recorded in the register of interests`
    AND `the duty`'s `it was brought to the attention of the member presiding at the meeting`

DECLARE DisclosureContent HAS
    `the nature of the interest is stated` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the monetary value can be quantified` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the monetary value is stated` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the extent of the interest is stated` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the content` IS A DisclosureContent
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the details disclosed meet section 25(2)` IF
        `the content`'s `the nature of the interest is stated`
    AND (    (    `the content`'s `the monetary value can be quantified`
              AND `the content`'s `the monetary value is stated`)
         OR  (    NOT `the content`'s `the monetary value can be quantified`
              AND `the content`'s `the extent of the interest is stated`))

§§ `26, 27 -- what an interested member may not do, and what happens if they do`

-- s 26: "A member ... who is interested in a relevant matter -- (a) MUST NOT VOTE or take part in
-- any discussion or decision of the public body or any committee relating to the matter, or
-- otherwise participate in any activity of the public body that relates to the matter; (b) must
-- WITHDRAW from any meeting ... during the consideration or discussion relating to the matter IF
-- THE MEMBER PRESIDING AT THE MEETING SO REQUESTS; (c) must NOT SIGN any document relating to the
-- entry into a transaction or the initiation of the matter; and (d) must be DISREGARDED FOR THE
-- PURPOSE OF FORMING A QUORUM for that part of a meeting ... during which a discussion or
-- decision relating to the matter occurs".
--
-- The withdrawal duty is triggered by the presiding member's request; it is not automatic. The
-- non-participation duty in (a) is automatic. If enough members are interested that the rest
-- fall short of the quorum, the body cannot decide the matter, and the Act contains no way
-- round: it gives the responsible Minister no power to act in the body's place.
GIVEN `the members present` IS A NUMBER,
      `of whom are interested in the matter` IS A NUMBER,
      `the quorum` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the members counted towards the quorum for that part of the meeting` IS
    `the members present` MINUS `of whom are interested in the matter`

GIVEN `the members present` IS A NUMBER,
      `of whom are interested in the matter` IS A NUMBER,
      `the quorum` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the body can decide the matter at this meeting` IF
    `the members counted towards the quorum for that part of the meeting` `the members present` `of whom are interested in the matter` `the quorum`
        AT LEAST `the quorum`

GIVEN `the presiding member has requested the member to withdraw` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the interested member must withdraw` IF
    `the presiding member has requested the member to withdraw`

-- s 27(1): "A public body must notify its responsible Minister of a failure to comply with
-- section 25 or 26, and of the matters affected, as soon as practicable after becoming aware of
-- the failure."
-- s 27(2): "the exercise of any power or performance of any function of a public body by the
-- public body IS NOT AFFECTED merely because at the relevant time -- (a) a member failed to
-- disclose his or her interest ...; or (b) the public body failed to give notice under this
-- section."
--
-- THE REGIME HAS NO SANCTION. A member who fails to disclose or who votes while interested
-- commits no offence under this Act (the only offences in it are in ss 7, 8 and 38), the
-- decision stands (s 27(2)), and the only consequence is a duty on the body to report the
-- failure to the Minister -- a duty the Act also leaves unenforced, since a body's failure to
-- notify likewise does not affect its acts.
DECLARE Breach HAS
    `a member failed to comply with section 25 or 26` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the public body has become aware of the failure` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the breach` IS A Breach
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the public body must notify the responsible Minister` IF
        `the breach`'s `a member failed to comply with section 25 or 26`
    AND `the breach`'s `the public body has become aware of the failure`

GIVEN `the breach` IS A Breach
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the public body's decision is affected merely by the breach` IF
    FALSE

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `this Act makes a failure to disclose an interest an offence` IF
    FALSE

§§ `28 -- committees`

-- s 28(2): "An individual may not be appointed as a member of such a committee of a public body
-- unless, BEFORE APPOINTMENT, he or she discloses to the public body the details of any interest
-- the individual has at that time, or is likely to have, in matters relating to the committee".
-- s 28(3): ss 23 to 27 apply to the committee with modifications: disclosure to the responsible
-- Minister becomes disclosure to the public body; and the s 27 report goes to the public body
-- instead of the Minister.
DECLARE CommitteeAppointment HAS
    `the committee is one the constitutional Act allows the public body to appoint` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the individual disclosed their interests to the public body before appointment` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the appointment` IS A CommitteeAppointment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the individual may be appointed to the committee` IF
        `the appointment`'s `the committee is one the constitutional Act allows the public body to appoint`
    AND `the appointment`'s `the individual disclosed their interests to the public body before appointment`

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a committee member's disclosure of an interest in a matter the committee regulates goes to the responsible Minister` IF
    FALSE

§§ `30, 31, 32 -- how a public body decides`

-- s 30(1): a meeting may be held "(a) by a quorum of the members, being assembled together at the
-- time and place appointed; or (b) by means of audio, audio and visual, or electronic
-- communication, PROVIDED THAT -- (i) the public body RESOLVES that the meeting, or that all its
-- meetings, may be held by such means; (ii) ALL of the members who wish to participate have access
-- to the technology needed to participate; and (iii) a quorum of members can SIMULTANEOUSLY
-- communicate with each other throughout the meeting."
-- s 30(2): a member participating by such means "is taken to be present".
DECLARE RemoteMeeting HAS
    `the public body resolved that the meeting or all its meetings may be held by such means` IS A BOOLEAN
    `all of the members who wish to participate have access to the technology` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a quorum of members can simultaneously communicate throughout` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the meeting` IS A RemoteMeeting
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a meeting may be held by electronic means` IF
        `the meeting`'s `the public body resolved that the meeting or all its meetings may be held by such means`
    AND `the meeting`'s `all of the members who wish to participate have access to the technology`
    AND `the meeting`'s `a quorum of members can simultaneously communicate throughout`

-- s 31(1): "If -- (a) a public body resolves that this section applies to any particular matter or
-- all its matters; (b) ALL of the members ... for the time being are sent ... a document setting
-- out a resolution; and (c) a MAJORITY OF THOSE MEMBERS WHO ARE ENTITLED TO VOTE on the matter
-- sign or approve in writing a document containing a statement that they are in favour, a
-- resolution in those terms is taken to be passed at a meeting ... on the day that the last member
-- required for the majority signs or approves the document."
--
-- The majority is of the members ENTITLED to vote, not of those who respond and not of all
-- members. An interested member is not entitled to vote on the matter (s 26(a)), so is outside
-- the denominator; but all members, interested ones included, must be SENT the document. There is
-- no quorum requirement, and no requirement that anyone be given time or an opportunity to
-- discuss.
DECLARE CircularResolution HAS
    `the public body resolved that section 31 applies to the matter` IS A BOOLEAN
    `all of the members for the time being were sent the document` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the number of members entitled to vote on the matter` IS A NUMBER
    `the number of those who signed or approved in writing that they are in favour` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the resolution` IS A CircularResolution
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a majority of those entitled to vote have signed` IF
    (2 TIMES `the resolution`'s `the number of those who signed or approved in writing that they are in favour`)
        GREATER THAN `the resolution`'s `the number of members entitled to vote on the matter`

GIVEN `the resolution` IS A CircularResolution
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the resolution is taken to be passed` IF
        `the resolution`'s `the public body resolved that section 31 applies to the matter`
    AND `the resolution`'s `all of the members for the time being were sent the document`
    AND `a majority of those entitled to vote have signed` `the resolution`

-- s 32(1): where a public body may delegate, "unless in such Act it is otherwise expressly
-- provided, the power to delegate DOES NOT EXTEND TO THAT POWER TO DELEGATE."
-- s 32(2): a delegation "(a) does not affect or prevent the performance of any function by the
-- public body; and (b) is not affected by any change in the membership of the public body or of
-- any committee, or by any change in the chief executive or employee".
GIVEN `the constitutional Act expressly allows sub-delegation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the delegate may delegate further` IF
    `the constitutional Act expressly allows sub-delegation`

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a delegation stops the public body performing the function itself` IF
    FALSE

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a change of membership or chief executive ends a delegation` IF
    FALSE
